diagnostics/list-invariance.em:7:29: this is List[Int], but `mistaken` was declared as List[Float]
  var mistaken: List[Float] = whole
                              ^^^^^
A list keeps the element type it was built with, so one list type cannot stand in for another. Build the list with the type it needs, as in `var rates: List[Float] = [1, 2]`.
